# Nothing is needed for the web app: it talks to the Worker it is served from
# (client/worker/), on the same origin. See client/README.md for `wrangler dev`.
#
# A native build has no origin to ask, so it needs the Worker's address. For
# an EAS build it is an EAS environment variable (README.md, Android); for
# `npm run android` against a Worker, set it here. It is PUBLIC (EXPO_PUBLIC_
# means it ships in the app).
#
# No database URL, password or key ever goes in this file or anywhere in
# client/: the Worker reaches D1 and R2 through its bindings and holds no key.

# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE=https://business-japanese-test-practice.<you>.workers.dev
